{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310655,"nonce":"7g7TKdtRb71MLH2gaO/qHY65CQ0=","title":"RESOLVED 2026-08-28 by c0188c34 (classify lexical captures by scope). Kept for the repro and the diagnosis.","message":"**RESOLVED by `c0188c34` (fix(closures): classify lexical captures by scope).**\nAll four repros below now pass. Kept for the diagnosis and the repro shapes.\n\nWas: **A lambda nested in a lambda could not capture from the enclosing lambda.**\nCompile error: `[E0100] Captured variable SymbolId(N) not found in scope`\n(`ir/mir/expr/lambda.rs`, the `captured_values` loop).\n\n```haxe\nclass M {\n    static function main() {\n        var outer = function(x:Int) {\n            var inner = function(y:Int) { return x + y; };   // E0100\n            return inner(1);\n        };\n        Sys.println(outer(2));\n    }\n}\n```\n\nDiscriminated 2026-08-25 -- it is NESTING, not symbol identity:\n\n| case | result |\n|---|---|\n| inner captures enclosing LAMBDA's param | FAILS |\n| inner captures enclosing LAMBDA's local | FAILS |\n| lambda captures a real FUNCTION's param | works |\n| single lambda captures a method local | works |\n\nPuzzle for whoever picks this up: `lower_lambda_body` does `symbol_map.clear()`\nthen inserts the lambda's own params, and the inner closure's captures are read\nfrom `symbol_map` BEFORE `generate_lambda_function` runs -- so at the moment the\ninner closure is built, the enclosing lambda's params should be present. They\nare not. Suspect `save_state`/`restore` around nested lowering, or the inner\ncapture naming a different SymbolId than the enclosing param's.\n\n\nA closure reading an INSTANCE FIELD captured a synthetic `this`: AST lowering\nmints a fresh `this` symbol at every site needing an implicit receiver\n(`ast_lowering/expr/mod.rs`, the `is_instance_field` branch), and that symbol is\nnever bound to a register. `mir/expr/variables.rs` already redirects a\n`this`-named symbol to `SymbolId(0)`; the capture path now does too.\n\nCorpus effect: of 23 tests failing with an unfound capture, 11 got past it and\n3 reached PASS. The remaining 12 are the nested case above.\n\nRelated: [[bugs-preexisting-ranked-2026-08-10]] #3 (closure + static var).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_nested_lambda_cannot_capture_from_enclosing_lambda` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}